{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:InformationTheory.PVsNpBoundary","@type":"LeanModule","name":"InformationTheory.PVsNpBoundary","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":40,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.both_topologically_obstructed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.both_topologically_obstructed","kind":"theorem","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L274-L278","doc":"Both parallels have nonzero topological invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.computationalParallel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.computationalParallel","kind":"def","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L265-L272","doc":"The computational obstruction parallel.\n(Using crossing number c = 3 as minimal nontrivial example;\nthe Skein degree is c² - 1 = 8.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.nsParallel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.nsParallel","kind":"def","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L249-L263","doc":"The NS obstruction parallel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.ObstructionParallel.classical_obstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.ObstructionParallel.classical_obstruction","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L247-L247","doc":"At `q = 1` (classical limit), the obstruction is visible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.ObstructionParallel.q_regularized","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.ObstructionParallel.q_regularized","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L245-L245","doc":"At `q > 1`, the q-deformation regularizes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.ObstructionParallel.top_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.ObstructionParallel.top_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L243-L243","doc":"The topological invariant is nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.ObstructionParallel.topological_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.ObstructionParallel.topological_invariant","kind":"def","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L241-L241","doc":"The topological invariant (χ for NS, deg P_L for computation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.ObstructionParallel.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.ObstructionParallel.mk","kind":"ctor","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L239-L239","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.ObstructionParallel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.ObstructionParallel","kind":"structure","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L229-L247","doc":"The unified picture:\n- NS obstruction depends on χ(A) (topological)\n- Computational obstruction depends on deg P_L (topological)\n- Both use the perpetual obstruction (complementary subgroups); for the\n  NS side this is withdrawn: the Kummer obstruction on Bring's surface\n  vanishes for `n ∣ 6` (re-scoped 2026-11-15, PR #7747, bean `qou-lx8f`)\n- Both are resolved at the q-scale (q > 1)\n- Both are open at the classical limit (q → 1)\n\nThis structure captures the parallel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.nontorsion_full_tree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.nontorsion_full_tree","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L218-L225","doc":"At non-torsion q, the Hecke algebra is semisimple: trivial radical.\nNo resolution paths are pruned; the full 3^c tree survives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.NonTorsionReal.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.NonTorsionReal.q","kind":"def","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L214-L214","doc":"The substrate parameter value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.NonTorsionReal.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.NonTorsionReal.mk","kind":"ctor","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L212-L212","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.NonTorsionReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.NonTorsionReal","kind":"structure","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L211-L214","doc":"A non-torsion real number: q > 1 and q^k ≠ 1 for all k ≥ 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.TorsionPoint.order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.TorsionPoint.order","kind":"def","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L193-L193","doc":"The order of the root of unity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.TorsionPoint.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.TorsionPoint.mk","kind":"ctor","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L191-L191","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.TorsionPoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.TorsionPoint","kind":"structure","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L188-L193","doc":"At a root of unity q = e^(2πi/n), the Hecke algebra has a\nnontrivial radical of codimension ≤ n^m (polynomial in n).\nThe radical prunes the resolution tree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.finite_field_p_eq_np","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.finite_field_p_eq_np","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L180-L184","doc":"Over a finite field, the asymptotic complexity class is P = NP:\nfor any fixed p, the lookup table has constant size (dependent on p). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.finite_field_always_decidable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.finite_field_always_decidable","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L164-L178","doc":"Over a finite field of size p, every function on {0, ..., 3^c - 1}\nis computable in at most p · 3^c steps.  This is polynomial in\nthe field size (though exponential in c).\n\nKey point: the obstruction ALWAYS vanishes over finite fields\nbecause the computation can be done by lookup table. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.obstruction_implies_boundary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.obstruction_implies_boundary","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L146-L160","doc":"The three criteria are related: if the obstruction is nonzero\n(either component), then the boundary is non-empty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.bandwidthSaturated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.bandwidthSaturated","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L141-L144","doc":"**Information-theoretic criterion**: the effective tree size\nexceeds the polynomial bandwidth budget. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.obstructionNonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.obstructionNonzero","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L136-L139","doc":"**Cohomological criterion**: the Skein resolution obstruction\nκ_c^comp is nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.idealNontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.idealNontrivial","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L129-L134","doc":"**Ideal-theoretic criterion**: the horizon ideal h_c is nontrivial\niff there exist polynomial-time algorithms that reach the boundary\nand return 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.boundary_dichotomy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.boundary_dichotomy","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L111-L125","doc":"The boundary is empty iff it is not non-empty (classical logic). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:p-vs-np-boundary","label":"conj:p-vs-np-boundary","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.boundaryNonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.boundaryNonempty","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L107-L109","doc":"Boundary is non-empty: some problem instance defeats all polynomial bounds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.boundaryEmpty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.boundaryEmpty","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L103-L105","doc":"Boundary is empty: every problem instance has a polynomial extraction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.np_witness_exponential","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.np_witness_exponential","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L80-L91","doc":"The witness space grows exponentially. Stated for the canonical\n(default-field) problem `⟨c, hc⟩`, whose `witness_space_size` takes\nits default value `3 ^ c`; for an arbitrary `NPProblem` the field may\nbe overridden, so the bound is asserted of the default construction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.NPProblem.witness_space_size","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.NPProblem.witness_space_size","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L78-L78","doc":"The witness space is exponential. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.NPProblem.has_verifier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.NPProblem.has_verifier","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L76-L76","doc":"**There exists a polynomial-time verifier**: the verification\ncost is bounded by a polynomial in the problem size — `∃ d`,\n`verify_steps ≤ (crossings + 1) ^ d`. This encodes the genuine\n\"poly-time verifier\" content of NP (replacing a vacuous\n`: True` field per AGENTS.md §3b-tax). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.NPProblem.verify_steps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.NPProblem.verify_steps","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L70-L70","doc":"The cost (in Planck steps) of verifying a proposed witness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.NPProblem.crossings_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.NPProblem.crossings_pos","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L68-L68","doc":"The problem is non-trivial: at least one crossing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.NPProblem.crossings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.NPProblem.crossings","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L66-L66","doc":"Number of crossings (problem size). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.NPProblem.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.NPProblem.mk","kind":"ctor","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L64-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.NPProblem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.NPProblem","kind":"structure","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L62-L78","doc":"The class NP: problems where a witness can be verified in poly time,\nbut finding the witness may require exponential time. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.classP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.classP","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L57-L60","doc":"The class P: problems where the computational boundary is empty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.ComplexityClass.decidable_in_poly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.ComplexityClass.decidable_in_poly","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L55-L55","doc":"The predicate: whether a given tree size admits polynomial extraction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.ComplexityClass.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.ComplexityClass.mk","kind":"ctor","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.ComplexityClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.ComplexityClass","kind":"structure","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L51-L55","doc":"A complexity class determined by the emptiness of the computational\nboundary.  Abstractly: a predicate on resolution trees. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.q_param","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PvsNPBoundary.R_q","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-vs-np-boundary.lean#L43-L45","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}